# origin/main behaviour (baseline per maintainer decision 6)
# Generated by TestLegacyMenuBackup (pkg/characterization); regenerate with -update. Do not edit.
# Screen: Backup (main menu 5), backups on, 2 (path) "backups", then q (pkg/menu), run in a child process
# Script: stdin "2\nbackups\n\nq\n", not a terminal, so nothing typed is echoed
# Start: enableBackups true, backupPath $TMP/var/backups/hardn (an empty directory), dryRun false
# Pauses: 1 ("Press Enter to ..."; origin/main says "Press any key to ...", DEV-050)
# KNOWN-DEFECT: A relative path is taken and saved: no check but the directory's (backup_manager.go:46-56). pkg/host/backup's Open refuses a relative backupPath (ErrSettings), which every engine plan checks (backup.Check) and every apply opens, so the session's next engine change, and every one after a start that reads this file, is refused (docs/engine/gallery-backup.md §6).
# KNOWN-DEFECT: The whole configuration is saved to ./hardn.yml, not to the file loaded (side-effects.md row 29).
# NOTE: The repository's calls are on the legacy mock file system; on a host they are real (infrastructure.ServiceFactory gives it the OS file system). The relative path is under the child's working directory, the temp dir.
